[CR CR1053 for 36.423] Reason for change: In case of SN-terminated bearers, one of the actions the MN may take in case the COUNT reaches its max value is to release the bearer and possibly set it up anew. To do so, it should be informed that the PDCP Count is reaching the max value. Summary of change: The Cause list is extended to add a proper value that can be used by the en-gNB when it indicates a bearer must be released. Consequences if not approved: MN is not aware of the situation and will not react appropriately when the SN releases the bearer due to reaching max Count value.

