rified, e.g., which bits are used to identify the PDCP SN. Therefore, the format needs to be clarified to avoid misunderstanding. Thus, RAN3 shall rename the “MBS Initial HFN and Reference PDCP SN” IE in E1AP into “MBS PDCP COUNT”, and adjust its description into “Encoded in the same format as the initialRX-DELIV IE and to be taken into account to configure the UE, as specified in the TS 38.331 [10]” Summary of change: Rename the “MBS Initial HFN and Reference PDCP SN” IE in E1AP into “MBS PDCP COUNT”, and adjust its description into “Encoded in the same format as the initialRX-DELIV IE and to be taken into account to configure the UE, as specified in the TS 38.331 [10]”. Impact Analysis: This CR has an isolated impact towards the previous version of the specification, and will not cause non-backward compatible issues. Consequences if not approved: The E1AP spec is misaligned with RRC spec.

